-- Barrier granularity (decision record; ex13/ex49 ruling): `~` is a new statement and a new barrier over the SAVED mask. Twin of s10-barrier-granularity.bqn.
-- The despawn applies to the mask saved at the spawn's gather, zero-padded over the minted rows: both ghosts survive even though they match Nord & Dead.
-- Barrier two's gather observes barrier one's scatter (8 rows exist); it is the effect's subject that is frozen, not the world.
-- The re-gather counterexample (idW/ghostW, zero ghosts) is BQN-only; this twin pins the saved-mask post-state.
--! registry ../registries/s10-barrier-granularity-a.reg
--! expect-n 6
--! expect keys = 1 2 4 5 6 7
--! expect nord = 1 0 0 0 1 1
--! expect ghost = 0 0 0 0 1 1

Nord & Dead , spawn Ghost
~
